course: dictionary
lesson: 2733
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word direct can mean different things, so context tells you which meaning fits. «Direct speech is the exact words someone says; it goes inside inverted commas, also called speech marks.» Here direct means exact, word for word.
explain: «Most bills leave the bank account by themselves, by direct debit, so the money seems to vanish without anyone paying at a till.» Here the money leaves the account by itself, with no one paying it by hand. Direct debit is a fixed phrase, so learn it as a whole.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If you swap in straight and it sounds wrong, look for a different meaning, such as plain, exact or to show the way.
fact: Direct means going straight from one place to another without stopping or turning, as in a direct flight.
fact: Direct means with nothing or nobody in between, as in direct sunlight or direct contact.
fact: A direct person says exactly what they mean, plainly.
fact: To direct someone means to tell or show them the way. To direct a film or play means to be in charge of the actors.
fact: «Direct speech» is the exact words someone says, inside speech marks.
exercise: «Can you direct me to the station?» What does direct mean here? | To fly without stopping | To make a film | To aim something at someone | *To show someone the way
exercise: «Direct speech is the exact words someone says, inside speech marks.» What is direct speech? | Words spoken very loudly | *The exact words someone says | A speech given by the head teacher
exercise: «A direct flight» goes from one place to another. What does direct mean in this phrase? | Flies in a circle | Stops at lots of airports | Flies only at night | *Goes straight, without stopping or turning
test: «Never look directly at the sun.» What does directly mean here? | *Straight at it, with nothing in between | Quickly, with a shout | Slowly, behind a cloud
test: «His question was directed at me.» What does directed at mean? | *Aimed at me | Asked by my friend | Sent away from me | Written down for me later
exam: «A direct debit is an automatic payment from a bank account that pays a bill on time each month.» What is a direct debit? | *An automatic payment from a bank account | A coin dropped in a box | A letter from the bank
